flowchart TB
  accTitle: BDI intention cycle
  accDescr: Beliefs describe what the agent takes to be true and desires describe wanted outcomes. Deliberation selects an intention. The intention constrains plan execution until observations and the applicable commitment policy justify continuation, reconsideration, or release.
  B[Beliefs: current world model] --> D[Desires: wanted outcomes]
  D --> F[Filter and deliberate]
  B --> F
  F --> I[Selected intention]
  I --> P[Plan and act]
  P --> O[Observe environment]
  O --> B
  O --> R{Commitment condition?}
  R -->|retain| I
  R -->|reconsider| F
  R -->|release| X[End this intention]
  classDef source fill:#EAF4FB,stroke:#1A4A8A,color:#1C1C1E
  classDef process fill:#F4F4F4,stroke:#888888,color:#1C1C1E
  classDef output fill:#EEF7EE,stroke:#27AE60,color:#1C1C1E
  classDef caution fill:#FEF9E7,stroke:#F39C12,color:#1C1C1E
  class B,D source
  class F,P process
  class I,O output
  class R,X caution
